  "summary": "Sets explicit `permissions: contents: read` on the main GitHub Actions CI workflow. This restricts the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` to read-only repository contents access across all CI jobs.",
  "problem": "CI permissions currently rely on Bitcoin Core's repository-level default setting. In contributor forks where repository defaults might permit broader write permissions, CI runs could execute with unnecessary token privileges.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: \"On this repository the token is already read-only, through the repository's default. The workflow's permissions key then adjusts that default... so the setting now lives in the workflow.\"",
    "Author references an identical hardening change in libsecp256k1 (bitcoin-core/secp256k1#1964)."
